  "version": "1.5.6",
  "notes": "## What's new in v1.5.6\n\n## 🚀 New\n\n- Project Doctor now checks Android setups: projects with an Android export preset or Gradle build template get checks for the Android SDK (platform tools, build tools, command-line tools), the Java JDK version, the debug keystore, release keystores and the Android build template. Projects that only look mobile (Mobile renderer, ETC2/ASTC textures, screen orientation, touch emulation) get the same checks as notes, since many desktop games use the Mobile renderer too\n- Tests and lint in Build & Export: run GUT or gdUnit4 tests headless, gdlint, or a gdformat check with one click. Output streams to the built-in console, and Stop ends the run\n- New Addons window in the project menu lists every addon in res://addons with its version, author and whether it is enabled, and checks the Godot Asset Library for newer versions. Addons installed through GodotHub are matched exactly; others are matched by name. Updating moves the old addon folder to the Trash and restores it if the update fails\n- Windows: right-click GodotHub in the taskbar to open recent projects from the Jump List. macOS: right-click the Dock icon for the same list\n\n## 🐛 Fixes\n\n- Choosing a project under Open Recent in the tray menu now opens it. Before, nothing happened\n- Templates in your template scan folder now sync automatically at startup, when files in that folder change, and after pulling a cloud sync. Before, they only synced when you pressed Sync\n- Project sizes no longer stay out of date after files deep inside a project change\n- Project icons now update when you replace the icon file itself\n- The splash screen loading bar no longer flickers rapidly when Reduce Motion is on\n- The onboarding intro animation no longer keeps running in the background after you leave it\n- Fixed window and Discord status listeners that could be left behind after their part of the app closed\n\n## ✨ Improvements\n\n- Faster startup: only the language you use is loaded, and rarely used dialogs load when first needed. The startup code is about half its previous size\n- The app stays smooth while Godot versions download. Download progress no longer redraws every page\n- Asset Library downloads send progress updates far less often and write to disk faster\n- Godot and export template downloads and installs use buffered disk access\n- Network requests share one connection pool and use compression, so GitHub and other online lookups respond faster\n- The Templates and Vault pages load their lists without briefly freezing the window\n- Project cards, the versions list and running-project timers redraw less often, which makes hovering and scrolling lighter\n- Status dot pulses, card entrance animations and tooltips use less GPU and CPU while looking the same\n- Background checks (git auto-fetch, console and export updates) pause while the window is hidden, and news and contributors are cached instead of fetched on every visit\n- Smaller and faster release builds",
